## Skills & delegation tooling â€” `agent-cooperation/`

- [Workflow review 2026-09-12](agent-cooperation/workflow-review-2026-09-12.md) â€” storage (ask IT for rclone OneDrive consent, else a manifest handoff through the sync client), compute routing as hypotheses with an outcome log, blindness levels instead of a species rule, 25 repos to archive and 2 to delete, six force multipliers; reviewed by Astra, Kimi, Grok with their objections recorded.
- [Clear writing](agent-cooperation/clear-writing/SKILL.md) â€” house prose style for everything written for humans (replies, docs, reports, emails, PR text), distilled 2026-08-22 from the full Google developer documentation style guide with Caleb's overrides on top (code comments stay Caleb-style; deliverable-polish minimalism wins in deliverables; explain-outside-core-domains wins when writing to Caleb). Invoke before writing any substantial prose. Install per machine by copying to `~\.claude\skills\clear-writing\`.
- [Build RRL Customer-Profile Decks](agent-cooperation/build-rrl-customer-profile-decks/SKILL.md) â€” reusable PowerPoint skill with the audited source deck bundled as an asset and a full design specification; duplicate inherited slide frames rather than rebuilding from the master.
- [Codex delegation](agent-cooperation/codex-delegation/SKILL.md) â€” **per-session working style**: invoke `/codex-delegation` to have Fable orchestrate while Codex (Sol) implements via the `codex` MCP server (registered user-scope, deferred; `mcp__codex` allowed). Not a standing default; composes with efficient-fable. Setup + full history in the [runbook](agent-cooperation/codex-delegation-runbook.md).
- [Deliverable-polish skill](agent-cooperation/deliverable-polish/SKILL.md) â€” the pre-ship pass from [[deliverable-verbosity]]: strip AI tells, cap bonus content at one, plain labels, process detail out of the artifact. Canonical copy here; install per machine by copying to `~\.claude\skills\deliverable-polish\`.
- [Efficient-fable skill](agent-cooperation/efficient-fable/SKILL.md) â€” rewritten 2026-09-12: keep Fable's context small (context scout: an Opus subagent triages files and returns only relevant excerpts), always pass `model`. Since 2026-09-26 Opus 5.5 is the default for every delegation, scans and triage included, and Sonnet is only for pure inventory or when Caleb asks. Also session-shape rules, plan-review council gate, routing-log habit. Synced by `agent-setup` since 2026-09-26. Canonical copy here; install per machine by copying the folder to `~\.claude\skills\efficient-fable\`.
- [Memory librarian skill](agent-cooperation/memory-librarian/SKILL.md) â€” `/memory-librarian`: an Opus subagent at max effort turns `.librarian/proposals/` (written by the session-end hook) into memory files and index lines, fixes wikilinks, dedupes and compacts indexes, flags contradictions; Fable reviews the diff. `librarian_check.py` is the health check (run it when in doubt).
- [Session hooks](agent-cooperation/hooks/README.md) â€” SessionStart prints one status line (week %, 5h %, fable weekly %, last session's avg context, HANDOFF.md age, an `atlas/` folder if the repo has one, pending librarian proposals with a `run /memory-librarian` nudge, uncarded specimen candidates); SessionEnd detaches a worker that logs session stats to `~/.claude/session-stats.jsonl`, drafts `HANDOFF.md` on Opus 5 at max effort for sessions of 6+ turns in a git repo, and writes a memory proposal to `.librarian/proposals/`. Installed per machine with `install-hooks.ps1 -Apply` (home desktop 2026-09-12). Recursion guard: `CLAUDE_SESSION_HOOK_WORKER`.
- [Claude usage MCP server](agent-cooperation/claude-usage-mcp/README.md) â€” `claude-usage` stdio server (Node, the same SDK and registration pattern as codex-mcp) with one read-only `get_usage` tool that returns the five-hour, weekly, and Fable-scoped weekly meters as a JSON digest; the `claude-usage` skill says when to call it. Built 2026-10-12 with an Astra and Kimi plan review and Sol and Grok code reviews. Per machine: `npm ci`, `npm test`, then `node register.mjs` with Claude Code closed. Fallback without registration: `node src/cli.mjs --summary`.
- [Plan-review council](agent-cooperation/plan-review/README.md) â€” `plan-review.ps1 -Spec plan.md` fans a spec out to Astra, Kimi, and Grok in parallel and collects `council.md`; synthesis stays with Fable. Risk-triggered: trust boundaries, destructive ops, schema changes, shipped numbers, loose requirements.
- [Delegation outcome log](agent-cooperation/routing-log/README.md) â€” `log_task.py` appends one row per model per task (shape, role, blindness, findings real/false/unique, rework); `summarize.py` shows which models earn their keep per shape. 244 rows over 82 tasks as of 2026-09-26, 49 of them backfilled from the 2026-08-30..09-09 data points. Routing rules are hypotheses this log corrects.
- [Machine manifests](context/machines/README.md) â€” `audit-machine.ps1` writes `context/machines/<COMPUTERNAME>.json` (tool versions, Docker + sandbox image state, `.env` key names, rclone remotes, skills). Generated; the source of truth for what a box can do. `-StartDocker` launches Docker Desktop when down.
- [Calibration specimens](agent-cooperation/calibration-specimens/README.md) â€” the benchmark set that reviewer models are scored against (`score.py`, results in the routing log). Sessions add candidate stubs to `_candidates/` before a fix lands. Pipeline and current state: [specimen-promotion-pipeline.md](context/reference/specimen-promotion-pipeline.md).
- [Statistical thinking framework](agent-cooperation/statistical-thinking/README.md) â€” built 2026-09-12: a router skill (`statistical-thinking`, the living loop: check what's on hand, research or add, test, retrospective) plus six skills (`stats-assumptions`, `stats-design`, `stats-compare`, `stats-data-quality`, `stats-uncertainty`, `stats-visual-inference`), a cited library with a lab annex and house priors, a Python toolkit, and 14 known-defect scenario tests. Domain-neutral core; RRL numbers are priors to re-measure. Read `SPEC.md` for the contracts; run `uv run --project toolkit pytest tests`.
