# AI usage and Tasks tabs (2026-10-17)

Spec, design candidates, and review record live in the code repo:
`in_out_button/docs/2026-10-17-usage-and-tasks-tabs-spec.md`,
`docs/design/2026-10-17-candidates/`, and the `.review/` folders beside the
spec. Handoff: `in_out_button/HANDOFF.md`, post-review commit `9a8ca7e`
(2026-10-17).

## What a future session must not undo

- The Claude credentials file is read on every call and never written or
  refreshed; `claudeusagewin` (an older tray app in `~/Tools`) does refresh
  and rewrite it, and persistent-memory treats that as the cautionary example.
- Codex is driven through its own `app-server` so the app never holds a Codex
  token; Codex refreshes its own tokens and refresh tokens are single-use.
- Every external string passes `Scrub.Message` before a page or the log.
- `tasks.json` edits by agents follow `tasks/README.md`: bump `rev`, set
  `updated`, keep unknown fields. The app keeps unknown fields too (Opus
  review finding, fixed the same day).

## Rulings and preferences (Caleb, 2026-10-17)

- Tasks storage: a JSON file in persistent-memory under a root `tasks/`
  folder. "Works great for me."
- Usage view: burn pace tiles (candidate C) first, rings and fuses (A)
  second; A shipped because it was built when he said so.
- Tasks view: Planner grouped by progress (candidate A); B (three lanes)
  shipped first. Both are page-only changes on the same message contract.
- Wrap-up called right after the weekly usage reset: fresh-week compute is
  not spare compute.

## Facts learned

- `where.exe codex` lists the extensionless npm shim first and `codex.cmd`
  second; the native exe sits under the shim folder's
  `node_modules\@openai\codex\node_modules\@openai\codex-win32-x64\vendor\...\bin\codex.exe`.
- Codex's account reported only a weekly window (10080 min) and `planType`
  "prolite" on 2026-10-17; label windows by duration, never assume two.
- WebView2 honours `WEBVIEW2_ADDITIONAL_BROWSER_ARGUMENTS=--remote-debugging-port=N`
  with no code change, which let the integration be driven end to end from
  Node over the DevTools protocol.
- The app's amber (180,83,9) and red fail colorblind separation when
  adjacent; the pages use amber `#c48604`.

## Debt

Nullable reset times (a meter with null `resets_at` is dropped today; the
page shows a placeholder), a timeout test that cannot tell a tree kill from a
single kill, no fake-server tests for the Anthropic error paths, no
five-clone merge drill for `tasks.json`, Gemini via `agy -p /usage` now that
Antigravity CLI 1.4.2 is installed (sign-in pending; the running app sees
`agy` on PATH only after a relaunch), and a first usage read that should wait
for the repo scan (it timed out on a saturated machine at deploy and recovered
on the next scheduled read).

